{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On the platform's own trace the detour is exactly 3.52 km over a booked optimal of 10.4 km, or 33.85% - it clears the POL-RD-01 establishment gate (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km) and stops there; nothing in the record corroborates the rider's picture of a much longer Yio Chu Kang Road / Upper Thomson detour beyond that measured figure, and the trace that fixes it is complete (158 fixes, 10 s cadence, no gap above 10 s, largest step 108.4 m), so the excess is bounded at 3.52 km and no more.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-04011", "EV-TRIP-04011"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The deviation is measured but not MATERIAL: 33.85% is below the 50% percentage gate and 3.52 km is below the 8.0 km absolute gate under POL-RD-01, so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not triggered by materiality and the FULL_REFUND uplift in POL-RD-06(b), which requires a deviation that is both material and substantiated on this trip, is unavailable. The remedy is the POL-RD-02 partial and nothing more.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-04011", "EV-TRIP-04011"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if POL-RD-06 is consulted, the driver shows no repeat-deviation pattern: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 260, a ratio of 0.00 well below the 0.05 threshold and below the alternative three-flag test, so no balance is resolved against him, no uplift attaches and no driver-conduct referral follows. No other field on either profile is relied on, per POL-GEN-01.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-04011"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is arithmetic and cannot exceed 4.60: charged_total of 22.32 less the recomputed optimal-route fare of 17.72 - (3.80 + 0.75 x 10.4 + 0.28 x 19) x the 1.0 surge multiplier read from the fare_breakdown, plus the 0.80 platform fee, with no ERP, no surcharge, no waiting fee and no promo - leaves 4.60, and 4.60 is only 20.6% of the charge, far below the 90% share that would convert a partial into a full refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-04011", "EV-TRIP-04011"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's premise that this trip is 'usually about 16 bucks' is contradicted by the platform's own figures: the booked optimal distance and duration price the same journey at 17.72, so the 6.00 contested is anchored on a fare the evidence does not support and the maximum the policy can move is 4.60.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-04011"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on this trip engages the pass-through limb: no ERP gantry was charged, erp_lines is empty on both the optimal and off-optimal sides, tolls_erp is 0.00, and the 0.00 airport surcharge sits on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport - so no POL-RD-09 correction may be added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure, and any off-route ERP would in any event already be comprehended in it and could never be counted twice.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-04011"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.6,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both sides largely agree on the arithmetic, and on this record they are right. Your trip TRP-04011 (Compass One to Junction 8) was booked against an optimal route of 10.4 km / 19 min. The GPS trace EV-GPS-04011 measures the distance actually driven at 13.92 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff events — an excess of 3.52 km, or 33.85% of the booked route. That clears both POL-RD-01 establishment tests (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is not MATERIAL: 33.85% is below the 50% gate and 3.52 km is below the 8.0 km gate, so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not triggered and the FULL_REFUND uplift in POL-RD-06(b) does not apply. The trace is likewise not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 — 158 fixes at a 10-second cadence, largest gap 10 seconds, largest step 108.4 m — so the measurement stands on the trace alone and needs no corroboration. The driver's explanation ('I followed the navigation app') does not move the figure: the bundle's only advisory, EV-ADVIS-04011-01, is MISSING (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0), so the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run, that clause is unavailable, and under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13 the assertion reduces nothing and supplies no amended optimal. No refund is excluded for a rider-requested detour: the chat log holds two messages, neither a detour request, neither naming a road, neither carrying a waypoint_hint, so the POL-RD-04 test cannot be run and the clause is unavailable. No pickup or dropoff was amended (both amendment timestamps null), so POL-RD-05 has nothing to re-quote and the booked optimal of 10.4 km / 19 min stands. The refund is therefore arithmetic under POL-RD-02, and because the fare is METERED (quoted_fare_sgd null) POL-RD-11 does not close the distance route. recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 10.4 km + 0.28 x 19 min) x 1.0 surge, the multiplier read from EV-FARE-04011, + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP + 0.00 surcharge + 0.00 waiting fee - 0.00 promo = 17.72. Refund = charged_total 22.32 - 17.72 = 4.60, above the 0.50 de minimis floor and 20.6% of the charge, well short of the 90% that would make it a full refund. No ERP gantry, toll or surcharge was charged, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing on top and nothing is counted twice. The rider's request for $6 is a round-figure estimate rather than a measured figure; the measured entitlement is SGD 4.60 and that is the sum awarded. No referral fires: there is no material deviation or repeat pattern for POL-RD-06(c), and no billing-integrity failure for POL-RD-09(4). Outcome: PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 4.60 to the rider. That amount is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so it executes on issue. This ruling is provisional; either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The absent advisory does not convert this case into an escalation. The driver names no evidence id for any advisory, so the missing advisory is not 'an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact' within POL-RD-10(5): an assertion that cites no artifact cannot be invoked against one, and an artifact no party has cited is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction in it. Under POL-RD-13 the deviation stands at the measured figure and POL-RD-02 runs against the booked optimal route, on the money track.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-04011-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

