    "explanation": "To both parties. This was a metered trip (fare_model METERED on EV-FARE-04011, quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not close the distance route). The booked optimal route from Compass One to Junction 8 was 10.4 km / 19 min (EV-TRIP-04011, platform router at booking). The GPS trace (EV-GPS-04011) measures the driven route at 13.92 km between the recorded start (11:26:40) and end (11:52:49) - 3.52 km and 33.85% over optimal. Both POL-RD-01 tests pass (more than 20% and more than 0.8 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED, and I take the trace figure as governing: trip_record.actual_distance_km 13.9 is only a rounded copy of the same measurement. The excess is below 50% and below 8.0 km, so it is not a MATERIAL deviation; the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not engaged by materiality, and in any event driver D-3315 shows no repeat pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 260), so no rider-favourable balance, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral follow. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 158 fixes at a 10-second cadence, largest interval 10 s, largest straight-line step 108.4 m - so the deviation stands on the trace alone and needs no independent corroboration. On the driver's explanation: 'I followed the navigation app' is an assertion that cites no artifact, and the only traffic advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-04011-01, is MISSING (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0, no payload). Under POL-RD-13 the driver named no advisory identifier, so this is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact under POL-RD-10(5); it is an uncited assertion that under POL-RD-08 neither reduces the measured excess nor supplies an amended optimal. I also note the driver's counterparty statement carries no weight multiplier and adds nothing the trace does not already show. On rider-side exculpations: the chat log (EV-CHAT-04011) holds two messages, neither a detour request, neither with a waypoint_hint and neither naming a road, so POL-RD-04 cannot be run and no distance is excluded; and pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null with amended_optimal_distance_km null, so POL-RD-05 has no re-quote to apply. The remedy is arithmetic under POL-RD-02: recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 10.4 km + 0.28 x 19 min) x 1.0 surge (read from EV-FARE-04011, the only artifact carrying that field) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP + 0 fixed surcharge + 0 waiting - 0 promo = 17.72. Refund = charged_total 22.32 - 17.72 = 4.60, above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and only 20.6% of the charge (not the 90% that would convert this to a full refund). No ERP gantry, toll or airport surcharge line exists, so no POL-RD-09 pass-through correction is added on top (and any off-route ERP would already be comprehended in the 4.60). The fare_breakdown shows 13.92 km billed against a 13.92 km trace, so there is no unbilled-distance shortfall and no POL-RD-04 driver compensation. The rider's '$6 back' is a round-figure estimate of what the detour cost; the measured entitlement on this record is SGD 4.60, which leaves the rider paying the 17.72 price of the route booked rather than the 22.32 charged for the 13.92 km driven. The rider's profile history does not raise the bar (deviation_claims_60d 1, below the figure of 4 that POL-RD-08 uses) and no context-only profile field was used as a ground. The monetary effect (4.60) is at or below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue subject to the appeal route under POL-GEN-04. One rider claim, about the absent advisory and POL-RD-10(5), was discarded by the referee for citing an impaired artifact without naming its issue code."
