    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this is a route deviation, and the refund is fixed by the policy arithmetic rather than by what either side asks for. Both advocates read the record the same way and I agree with them.\n\nWHAT THE EVIDENCE SHOWS. The trip record (EV-TRIP-04011), the GPS trace (EV-GPS-04011) and the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-04011) all carry trip id TRP-04011 and align to the second on the 11:26:40 start and the 11:52:49 finish. The GPS trace measures the distance actually driven at 13.92 km; under POL-RD-01 that trace figure governs, and the trip record's 13.9 km is a rounded copy of the same measurement and is not used for the threshold test. The booked optimal route was 10.4 km and 19 minutes. The excess is therefore 3.52 km, or 33.85% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass — the excess is greater than 20% of optimal and greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms — so the deviation is established.\n\nTRACE INTEGRITY. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes: 158 fixes at a 10-second cadence, no interval above 10 seconds, largest straight-line step 108.4 m. POL-RD-07(a) to (c) do not fire, so no down-weighting and no corroboration requirement arises.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S EXPLANATION. The driver's account ('I followed the navigation app; did not go the long way on purpose') cites no evidence id and no clause, so under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight and does not reduce the measured excess or supply an amended optimal route. The bundle's only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-04011-01, is MISSING — issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0, no payload — so the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run and the excuse is weightless under POL-RD-13. Because the driver named no evidence id for that advisory, its absence is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact within POL-RD-10(5), and the case is decided on the money track rather than escalated.\n\nNO RIDER-SIDE EXONERATION. POL-RD-04 does not apply: the chat log (EV-CHAT-04011) holds two messages, neither a detour request, neither carrying a waypoint_hint, and neither naming a road, so nothing is excluded from the excess. POL-RD-05 does not apply: pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null and the amended optimal fields are null, so the booked 10.4 km / 19 min stands as the baseline.\n\nTHE REMEDY. The trip is METERED (quoted_fare_sgd null), so POL-RD-11 does not close the distance route and POL-RD-02 runs. recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 10.4 km + 0.28 x 19 min) x 1.0 surge + 0.80 platform fee = 16.92 + 0.80 = 17.72. The 1.0 surge multiplier is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, the only artifact that carries the field. Refund = charged_total 22.32 - 17.72 = 4.60, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 = 4.60. That exceeds the 0.50 de minimis floor and is 20.6% of the charge, well short of the 90% that would convert a partial into a full refund. No ERP, toll, waiting or surcharge line exists, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing on top and nothing is double-counted.\n\nTHE RIDER'S $6. The $6 figure and the 'usually about 16 bucks' premise are not supported by the evidence: the platform's own optimal-route fare for this journey is 17.72, so the measured entitlement is 4.60.\n\nDRIVER COMPENSATION AND REFERRALS. No driver compensation arises: the rider was not billed for less distance than the trace records. No POL-RD-06 conduct pattern exists (deviation_flags_90d 0 against 260 completed trips in 90 days), so there is no conduct referral, and there is no billing-integrity defect to refer. The referrals list is empty.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND EXECUTION. The ruling rests only on weight-1.0 artifacts, so confidence is not capped below 1.0; I set it at 0.90. The monetary effect of SGD 4.60 is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so the refund executes automatically on issue, subject to the appeal route under POL-GEN-04. One rider claim was discarded at the mechanical check for citing the impaired advisory without disclosing its issue code; its substance is preserved by a separate kept claim that does disclose the impairment.",
